<v Heather Nixon>The first time I saw her, she looked at me and she goes, Heather, what the fuck? What the fuck, Heather? And I just went, I'm so sorry. And she was really-- it was hard. She was really, really raw. She was not OK.
<v Heather Nixon>我第一次见到她时，她看着我，她说，希瑟，这他妈是怎么回事？这他妈是怎么回事，希瑟？我只是说，我非常抱歉。她真的——这很难。她真的，非常痛苦。她当时不好。

00:45:29.910 --> 00:45:49.430
<v Heather Nixon>And I said to her, I said, listen, when you're ready, I'd love to just get some information from you. Because I'm going to take this beyond where we are right now. I said, I'm going to make sure that institutionally, this doesn't happen again. And I'm going to make sure that people hear about this and that this can be used for good.
<v Heather Nixon>我对她说，我说，听着，当你准备好了，我很想从你那里得到一些信息。因为我打算把它带到我们现在所处的范围之外。我说，我会确保从体制上讲，这种情况不会再发生。我会确保人们听到这件事，它可以被用于好的方面。

00:45:49.430 --> 00:46:03.840
<v Clara Hochhauser>She wasn't going to let it go and she was gonna take action. She was gonna do something to prevent this from happening again.
<v Clara Hochhauser>她不会让这件事过去，她会采取行动。她会做些什么来防止这种情况再次发生。

